TI  - Nonintubated Tracheal Surgery.
PG  - 91-99
LID - S1547-4127(19)30058-1 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.thorsurg.2019.08.008 [doi]
AB  - The article describes an anesthetic management strategy for resection of the 
      cervical trachea due to benign stenosis without using an endotracheal tube. The 
      strategy includes: (1) insertion of an airway stent in the stenotic area, (2) 
      insertion of a supraglottic airway device (SGAD), and (3) advancing a jet 
      ventilation catheter through the SGAD. The stent is removed during surgery 
      together with the resected part of the trachea. The technique of nonintubated 
      tracheal resection allows the surgeon to work most comfortably and helps the 
      anesthesiologist properly maintain the patient's vital functions in the operating 
      room.
