      tumour of uncertain malignant potential by a silicone OKI-stent™.
PG  - e00798
LID - 10.1002/rcr2.798 [doi]
LID - e00798
AB  - There is no standard treatment for smooth muscle tumour of uncertain malignant 
      potential (STUMP) but it usually has a good prognosis. Airway stenting is 
      performed to manage central airway patency. In the present case, it was no 
      treatment for STUMP, but performance status was good, so airway stenting was 
      performed.
