TI  - Bronchoscopy Laser and Silicone Y-Stents as Emergency Airway Management in 
      Central Airway Stenosis Due to Secondary Thyroid Carcinoma: A Case Report.
PG  - 6338073
LID - 10.1155/2022/6338073 [doi]
LID - 6338073
AB  - Total airway obstruction in thyroid cancer is rare and has high morbidity and 
      mortality. Airway management in such cases is challenging, especially in cases in 
      which thyroid masses cannot be totally resected. It is important to choose the 
      appropriate airway treatment modality. Currently, therapeutic rigid bronchoscopy 
      procedures and endoluminal lasers, as well as airway stent insertion, are a 
      management modality of near-total malignant airway obstruction. We report a rigid 
      bronchoscopy procedure combined with laser and Y-stent silicone insertion in 
      thyroid cancer with extension infiltration, as well as compression in the trachea 
      covering the subglottic tracheal area up to the main carina and 
      tracheo-bronchomalacia, manifesting as acute respiratory failure.
