DP  - 2023 Aug
TI  - A new treatment strategy for airway obstruction induced by a giant benign goiter: 
      A case report.
PG  - 376
LID - 10.3892/etm.2023.12075 [doi]
LID - 376
AB  - Severe respiratory distress induced by airway obstruction requires prompt 
      attention for restoration of normal function in the airway passage. A large 
      benign thyroid goiter that compresses the trachea is a rare occurrence. Emergency 
      thyroidectomy with dyspnea can increase the chance of surgical complications in 
      such cases. Here, a rare case of dyspnea induced by a large goiter is reported 
      and a safe and effective therapeutic strategy for treatment was demonstrated. 
      First, a self-expandable metal stent was placed to relieve airway obstruction. A 
      week later, total thyroidectomy under general anesthesia was performed. After 3 
      months, the metal stent was surgically removed. The findings of the present case 
      report demonstrated that life-threatening airway obstruction secondary to benign 
      goiter could be effectively treated by placing an airway stent, followed by 
      thyroidectomy.
