TI  - Incorporated airway stent: a useful option for treating tracheal stenosis after 
      metallic stenting.
PG  - 254-6
AB  - This study incorporated a silicone tracheal stent into a metallic stent in a 
      complicated airway stenosis patient. The silicone tracheal stent provided a 
      stable and patent airway. The patient was discharged smoothly after the 
      procedure. At 5 months after surgery, the patient remained stable and resumed all 
      daily activities without any respiratory symptoms.
